{
 "method_card": {
  "steps": [
   "Break each number into prime factors using a factor tree",
   "Write in index form (e.g. 2³ × 3 × 5)",
   "HCF: multiply shared primes with the LOWEST powers",
   "LCM: multiply ALL primes with the HIGHEST powers"
  ],
  "title": "Factors, Multiples & Primes",
  "content": "<p><strong>Factors</strong> of a number are whole numbers that divide into it exactly. <strong>Multiples</strong> are the results of multiplying a number by integers (its times table). <strong>Prime numbers</strong> have exactly two factors: 1 and themselves.</p><p>The <strong>Highest Common Factor (HCF)</strong> is the largest factor shared by two or more numbers. The <strong>Lowest Common Multiple (LCM)</strong> is the smallest number that appears in both times tables.</p><p>To find HCF and LCM efficiently, use <strong>prime factor decomposition</strong>: break each number into a product of prime factors using a factor tree. For HCF, multiply the shared primes with the lowest powers. For LCM, multiply all primes with the highest powers.</p><p>Remember: 1 is <em>not</em> a prime number (it has only one factor). The smallest prime is 2, and it's the only even prime.</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>Find the HCF and LCM of 24 and 36</strong></p><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> \\(24 = 2^3 \\times 3\\) and \\(36 = 2^2 \\times 3^2\\)</p><p><strong>Step 2 — HCF:</strong> Shared primes with lowest powers: \\(2^2 \\times 3 = 12\\)</p><p><strong>Step 3 — LCM:</strong> All primes with highest powers: \\(2^3 \\times 3^2 = 72\\)</p><p><strong>Answer:</strong> HCF = 12, LCM = 72</p>"
 },
